    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The `householdId` is now deterministic, and the full test suite passes: 13 tests, including the existing `AcceptanceTest` and 3 new ones I added.\n\n**What changed**\n- **How the ID is computed:** it's the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`. The last name is trimmed, runs of spaces are collapsed and it's lower-cased. It's set when the owner is created or updated, in `ClinicServiceImpl.householdIdOf` and `saveOwner`. The old `joinHousehold`, which matched on address and generated random IDs, is gone.\n- **Duplicate block:** creating an owner whose household already has members now returns 409 unless `sharesHousehold` is true. The 409 comes from a new `DuplicateHouseholdException`, and its response includes the `householdId`. The existing identity-key check also uses the computed ID.\n- **Declared members:** an owner created with `sharesHousehold` gets the same `householdId` and is never flagged as a possible duplicate (`possibleDuplicateOf` is null).\n- **Household size:** it's counted from the computed ID, because `saveOwner` sets the ID before counting.\n- **Docs:** I updated `openapi.yml` (the `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `possibleDuplicate` and 409 descriptions).\n- **Tests:** the new ones are in `HouseholdTest.java`. They check the exact hash, the 409 when `sharesHousehold` isn't set (including a different-case last name), and that a declared member is created without the duplicate flag.\n\n**Things you should know**\n- **No postcode means no `householdId`.** I left it null in that case so that owners with the same last name and no postcode aren't all treated as one household and blocked. If you'd rather hash an empty postcode, it's a one-line change in `householdIdOf`.\n- **`possibleDuplicate` is now always false in practice.** Possible duplicates are now matched by `householdId`, so an undeclared same-household owner is rejected with 409 and a declared one isn't flagged. The flag is effectively unreachable; I kept it rather than removing an API field.\n- **The membership level doesn't use household size.** `toMembershipLevel` only looks at email and namesakes, so there was nothing to change there. `householdSize` isn't returned by the API either.\n- **Seed owners** have a null `household_id` until they're next updated, so they don't trigger the duplicate block. Updates recompute the ID but don't apply the 409 check.",
